      <h3>Do link-based credits (Vultr $100, DigitalOcean $200) require a credit card?</h3>
      <p>Yes, both require a payment method at signup. The credit is applied against charges; you pay $0 for the first 30-60 days if usage stays under the credit limit. Cancel before the credit expires to avoid any post-credit charges. Vultr's $100 covers roughly 4 months of a $24/mo plan or 20 months of a $5/mo plan. DigitalOcean's $200 covers roughly 8 months of a $24/mo plan or 33 months of a $6/mo plan.</p>

      <h3>What's the catch with "lifetime discount" RackNerd promos?</h3>
      <p>The discount is locked to the initial billing term. If you buy a 1-year Special Promo at $21.99/year, the renewal price depends on whether that SKU is still listed when your term expires. Most annual Special Promos renew at the regular KVM catalog rate ($215.88/year for the 1 GB plan) once the promo SKU is retired. To stay on the promo rate, watch for RackNerd announcements about new Special Promos and renew during a promo window.</p>

